       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 3,200 mg/day for adults in a monitored setting. Single doses are typically 400\u2013800 mg.\n- **Risk:** the requested dose is twice the daily maximum. It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours, for pain or fever\n- 1600 mg as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note, or you can have pharmacy review it first. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it."
